return array(
	'title'       => 'Privacy Policy',
	'seo_title'   => 'Privacy Policy | Testnook',
	'description' => 'How Testnook handles your data: tests run on your device and a few share only an anonymous final score. How Google Analytics, cookies and ads are used.',
	'updated'     => '2026-10-29',
	'body'        => '<p>This policy explains what information testnook.com ("Testnook", "we", "us") collects and how it is used. The short version: <strong>the tests run on your device, and we never see your camera, microphone or anything you type into a test.</strong> A few tools share your final score anonymously so we can show site averages, and you can turn that off.</p>
<h2>Camera, microphone and input tests</h2>
<p>When a test needs your camera or microphone, your browser asks for your permission. The video and audio are processed only inside your browser on your own device. They are never sent to our servers or to anyone else, and they are not stored. If a test lets you make a short recording for playback, the recording is kept in your browser\'s memory and is deleted when you leave or reload the page.</p>
<p>Keyboard, mouse, controller, touch and sensor tests also run locally. The keys you press and the movements you make are not sent anywhere. The only exception is the final score of a few tests, described under <a href="#results">anonymous test results</a> below.</p>
<h2 id="network-tools">Internet speed, IP, DNS and WebRTC tools</h2>
<p>Some tools must talk to servers on the internet to work, and they do so directly from your browser, not through us. The <a href="/internet-speed-test/">internet speed test</a> and <a href="/ping-test/">ping test</a> exchange random test data with Cloudflare (speed.cloudflare.com); the ping test can also time requests to Google. <a href="/what-is-my-ip/">What is my IP</a> asks Cloudflare and ipify (api.ipify.org) which address your connection uses, and the internet registries (through rdap.org) who owns that address. The <a href="/dns-lookup/">DNS lookup</a> sends the domain you type to Cloudflare or Google DNS over HTTPS, and its speed test sends lookups for popular domains to eight public DNS providers. The <a href="/webrtc-leak-test/">WebRTC leak test</a> contacts STUN servers run by Google and Cloudflare. These services see your IP address while the request is made, as any website does, and handle it under their own privacy policies. The results are shown only in your browser: Testnook does not receive or store them. Your speed test history is kept in your browser\'s local storage and can be cleared on the page.</p>
<h2 id="results">Anonymous test results and site statistics</h2>
<p>On the click speed (CPS), reaction time, typing, mouse accuracy and dead pixel tests, your <strong>final score</strong> is sent to our server when a test ends, so that we can show how people score on average and tell you how your result compares. What is stored is the name of the test, the score (for example 6.8 clicks per second, 245 ms, 62 words per minute with 97% accuracy, or the area of the screen where you reported a bad pixel), whether the score passed our checks, and the date. We do not store your IP address, the time of day, your browser or device details, the text you typed, your clicks or anything else with the score, so a stored result cannot be linked back to you.</p>
<p>To stop abuse we keep a hashed form of your IP address for up to 24 hours, in a counter that limits how many results one connection can send. The hash changes every day and is never stored with a result. Results older than 400 days are reduced to monthly totals and deleted.</p>
<p>You can turn score sharing off with the <strong>Turn off</strong> link under any of these tools. The choice is saved in your browser\'s local storage and applies to every tool on this site until you turn it back on. Tools embedded on other websites never send results.</p>
<h2 id="leaderboards">Leaderboards and nicknames</h2>
<p>After a click speed, reaction time, typing or mouse accuracy test you can choose to add your score to a public <a href="/leaderboards/">leaderboard</a> under a nickname. This is optional. If you do, the nickname is stored with that score and shown publicly with the score and the date. Please use a nickname and not your real name. Nicknames are checked against a list of blocked words and may be hidden or removed by us at any time. A leaderboard entry is kept for as long as the leaderboards exist. To have a nickname removed, email us with the nickname, the test and the date; the score then stays as an anonymous result only.</p>
<h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
<p>Like almost every website, our hosting provider (Hostinger) keeps standard server logs, which include your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time of the request. These logs are used for security and to keep the site running, and are deleted on a rolling basis.</p>
<h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
<p>Google Analytics sets the cookies described under <a href="#analytics">analytics</a> below (outside the EEA, the UK and Switzerland). Apart from those, we store a small setting in your browser\'s local storage to remember whether you prefer light or dark mode. Some tools may also remember your own settings, such as screen calibration for the online ruler, your personal best scores and whether you turned score sharing off, in the same way. This data stays on your device.</p>
<h2 id="analytics">Analytics</h2>
<p>We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, a service from Google, to understand which pages and tests are used, where visitors come from and how fast the site works for them. Google Analytics collects information such as the pages you view, the page that sent you here, approximate location (city or country, worked out from your IP address, which Google does not store), browser and device type, screen size and how long pages take to load. It uses cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>) to tell a returning visitor from a new one. We see this only as aggregated reports; it does not identify you personally to us, and nothing from inside a test (camera, microphone, keys, clicks or scores) is sent to Google Analytics. If you press one of the <strong>Share your score</strong> buttons, Google Analytics records only that a share happened, which button was used and which test it was, never the score itself. The share buttons are plain links: no WhatsApp, X, Facebook or Reddit code is loaded on our pages, and nothing is sent to those services unless you choose to post. Data in Google Analytics is kept for the period set in our account (between 2 and 14 months) and then deleted.</p>
<p>In the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland, Google Analytics runs in Google\'s consent mode with analytics and advertising storage <strong>denied</strong> by default. It then sets no cookies and sends Google only anonymous, cookieless signals (such as a page view) that cannot recognize you on a later visit. Tools embedded on other websites do not load Google Analytics at all.</p>
<p>You can block Google Analytics with your browser\'s cookie or tracking settings, a content blocker, or the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>. We do not use Microsoft Clarity or any other analytics service at the moment.</p>
<h2>Advertising</h2>
<p>Testnook is free and is meant to be supported by advertising. Ads are <strong>not switched on</strong> at the moment. When they are enabled, we will use Google AdSense, and the following applies:</p>
<ul>
<li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
<li>Google\'s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
<li>You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors\' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>When ads are switched on, visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland will be shown a consent message first, before any personalized ads or analytics cookies are used, and will be able to change their choice at any time.</p>
<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Testnook is a general audience site and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal data held about you, or to object to its use. Because the tests do not send personal data to us, we usually hold nothing beyond standard server logs, aggregated Google Analytics reports, anonymous test scores that cannot be linked to you, and any email you send us. To make a request, contact us at the address below.</p>
<h2>Emails you send us</h2>
<p>If you email us, we use your address and message only to reply and to improve the site. We do not sell or share it.</p>
<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We will update this page when our practices change. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:' . esc_attr( TN_CONTACT_EMAIL ) . '">' . esc_html( TN_CONTACT_EMAIL ) . '</a>. Testnook is run by ' . esc_html( TN_FOUNDER_NAME ) . '.</p>',
